{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Unto Moses, etc.</b> The reason for calling Moses, according to them of blessed memory (Yalkut Shimoni) who said that they were ritually impure — He called Moses so that they would recognize the nature of the separation that Moses had maintained, such that he was prepared for HaShem to speak to him without any impediment, whereas they, though HaShem called them, could not go out. And according to the plain sense, it was so that Moses would be prepared to pray on behalf of Miriam. Further, the reason for calling Moses is because HaShem intended to reveal to them immediately, through the very order of the calling, that Moses was greater than they — for He preceded him before them in the calling and let them hear the thing. Through this they would feel a contradiction to their thought, which they had expressed: ״הֲרַק בְּמֹשֶׁה הֲלֹא גַּם בָּנוּ״, etc."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:08:06.825336074Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}